{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>For with a strong hand HaShem brought you out of here, and no leaven (chameitz) shall be eaten.</b> What has leaven to do with 'a strong hand'? Rather, Scripture comes to hint that leaven alludes to the attribute of judgment (midat ha-din). And since Israel attained 'the great hand,' which is the attribute of judgment, therefore He forbade and distanced from them leaven, hinting to them that they should distance themselves from believing in the attribute of judgment alone — that they should not cut the shoots (liqetzotz ba-nti'ot) and not believe that the attribute of judgment alone did this, for He, blessed be He, and His court were there. And this is what is written at the creation of the world: 'בראשית ברא אלהים' and afterward 'ביום עשות ה' אלהים.' And this is what the prophet said (Isaiah 48:13): 'אף ידי יסדה ארץ וימיני טפחה שמים' — He mentioned 'My hand' and afterward 'My right hand,' and the word 'אף' is like 'also (גם),' serving to include and to indicate that not the hand alone did this. Therefore it says: 'For with a strong hand HaShem brought you out' — for it was HaShem who brought them out, not the hand alone. And this is the reason for the prohibition of leaven by way of the Kabbalah. And from this matter Scripture punishes the one who eats leaven on Pesach with the penalty of karet — measure for measure — for every one who eats leaven on Pesach, behold, he is cutting the shoots; therefore: 'ונכרתה הנפש ההיא' etc. And understand this." "<b>And what</b> He said — <b>Remember this day</b> — this is a positive commandment to remember the Exodus from Egypt every day. And our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted (Deuteronomy 16:3): 'למען תזכור את יום צאתך מארץ מצרים כל ימי חייך' — 'ימי חייך' — the days; 'כל ימי חייך' — the nights. This is what our Rabbis of blessed memory said: 'אמת ואמונה' in the evening and 'אמת ויציב' in the morning — this is the remembrance by day and by night, which corresponds to the attribute of mercy (midat ha-rachamim) and the attribute of judgment (midat ha-din). And this is what it says: 'For with a strong hand' — the attribute of judgment — 'HaShem brought out' — the attribute of mercy. And this is what Moses hinted in his prayer (Exodus 32:11): 'אשר הוצאת מארץ מצרים בכח גדול וביד חזקה' — he explained that the Exodus was not by 'a strong hand' alone, but by 'great power' and by 'a strong hand.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 13, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:58:31.868643484Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}